    <fr:title text="Commutative-diagram animation macros">Commutative-diagram animation macros</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Authoring layer for declarative animated commutative diagrams. These macros
emit the DOM that <html:code>cd-anim.js</html:code> reads: objects are the free generators
(positions live in keyframes); edges are <html:em>derived</html:em> (geometry computed from
their endpoints each frame, so arrows are sticky/buffered/curved). Set the deck
to slide mode and import this file.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Usage.</html:strong> <html:code>cdanim</html:code> wraps a diagram; <html:code>cdobj</html:code> declares an object
(its label); <html:code>cdedge</html:code>/<html:code>cdcedge</html:code> declare a (curved) arrow by endpoint
ids; <html:code>cdkey</html:code> is a keyframe holding <html:code>cdat</html:code> placements (logical 0--100
coordinates). The runtime plays keyframe to keyframe over a fixed run time.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
